+valid only if every claim tuple under it would carry that same evaluation
+identity on itself. It never overrides a claim tuple's own evaluation
+identity: a claim that names a different evaluation invalidates the scope, an
+invalid scope is not emitted, and each claim then names its own. A scope
+carries the evaluation identity and nothing else. It never carries a label,
+tier, reason, freshness, challenge, review, draft or adoption state, an
+Unknown, a claim's own identity, or `non-citable` / `presentation-artifact`,
+each of which stays on the unit as this clause requires. A scope is expanded
+to one evaluation identity per claim before any parity comparison. The
+machine-queryable endpoints, every plain-text or exported rendering and any
+copy, share or export function the surface offers carry the evaluation
